        "raw": "<p>Depends how complex the system is... if it is almost entirely narrative then the sky is the limit in terms of crazy powers, cool skills and so on. If it is a streamlined combat based system well there are only so many ways to do damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Personally I was designing a game once that used multipliers of stats. For example Enhanced might be 1.5 the stat, Inhuman might be 2x the stat, Superhuman might be 3x and Ultra would be 4x. Cosmic was the max. So a kid (3) with super strenght would be less powerful than a body builder (6) with super strenght.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Example:</p><p>Gray Girl</p><p>Brawn: 4</p><p>Brains: 6</p><p>Skill: 5<br />&nbsp;</p><p>Enhanced Telekinesis(Brains). Range of Sight. Feats: Shield. Shield other.&nbsp; (So basically 9 Strenght TK)</p><p>Superhuman Telepathy (Brains). Range of Sight. Feats: Inflict pain. Comunicate. Confuse. Control.&nbsp; (So basically 18 points for Telepathy).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This could be used with die pools or pretty much any system.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
